            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0626" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-26T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 28—2:55
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>97. The following note received from the Haitian Government: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In response to the letter of this day from Your Excellency I am charged
                            to inform you that the Financial Adviser is authorized to sign the
                            contract of the loan of $16,000,000 in the name of the Haitian
                            Government and that the bonds of that loan can be put on sale
                            immediately after the signature of the contract.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
